# Act II
dialogue quill
  node root quill "You're the clerk. Licence and all. Don't get comfortable."
    > "I'm crew now." -> crew
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "You're the lookout who spots lies at two miles." if seen:tavernkeeper.crew and not seen:quill.marta -> marta
    > "I found your spyglass." if has spyglass and seen:quill.what -> lost
    > "What's ahead of us?" -> ahead
    > "Nothing. Carry on." -> bye
  node crew quill "Crew's what the captain writes in the book. You're cargo with opinions."
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "Fair enough." -> bye
  node marta quill "Marta. Of course. Did she mention compliments?"
    > "(Say nothing.)" -> learn
      add aff 1
    > "She did. I've been working on one." -> bite
  node learn quill "Good. You learn fast, for cargo."
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "I'll leave you to it." -> bye
  node bite quill "Keep trying. From over there."
    > "I need to see the captain." if not quill_helped -> captain
    > "Noted. I'll stay over here." -> bye
  node captain quill "She's aft. Past me. Crew only. And you're cargo."
    > "What would get me past?" -> what
    > "I found your spyglass." if has spyglass and seen:quill.what -> lost
    > "I'll find a way." -> bye
  node what quill "Be useful. Or find my spyglass. I dropped it on deck in the dark. I've been squinting since."
    > "Is this it?" if has spyglass -> lost
    > "I'll keep an eye out." -> bye
  node lost quill "That's mine. Never mind where. Give it here, and I'll forget I saw a clerk back here."
    > "Here. (give the spyglass)" -> thanks
      take spyglass
      set quill_helped
      note quill_spyglass "Quill dropped her spyglass on deck in the dark and would not let a clerk past without it. Returning it bought me the run of the aft deck."
    > "Not yet." -> bye
  node thanks quill "There she is. Dented twice, still honest. …You're blurrier up close. Captain's in her cabin, under the wheel."
    > "Thank you, Quill." -> thanked
      add aff 1
    > "I'll put in a good word with the captain." -> goodword
  node thanked quill "Thank the deck. It nearly ate it. And the captain doesn't hear about this."
  node goodword quill "Put in a good word for yourself. You'll need it. And not a word about this."
  node ahead quill "Fog, then the Straits. Then whatever's emptying ships out there. The insurers call it weather."
    > "And you?" -> you
    > "Good to know." -> bye
  node you quill "I call it rude. Weather doesn't take the crew and leave the dinner on. I'm only the lookout. For now."
    > "For now?" -> ambition
    > "Good to know." -> bye
  node ambition quill "Our navigator died last winter. Somebody has to read the stars. Might as well be someone who can see them."
    > "Navigators get written in the log. I've filed a thousand." -> filed
      add aff 1
    > "Good luck." -> bye
  node filed quill "Lookouts get written in too. Under “and others”. …Off you go."
  node bye quill "Off you go. And stop standing like that. You're making the mast nervous."
  # Pell's sextant, given with the captain's terms in hand (rooms.ts, marrow_deck).
  node sextant narrator "She takes the sextant in both hands, like something that might be taken back."
    -> swear
  node swear quill "Pell's. …You want me to swear to your line."
    > "I want the captain to hear it from a navigator." -> lookout
    > "I want my sums checked. You seem the type." -> sums
  node sums quill "I am the type. But Vane won't take a lookout's word on the reef. I'm a lookout."
    > "Not in the log, you're not." -> write
      add aff 1
    > "You're the best eyes on this ship." -> eyes
  node lookout quill "I'm a lookout."
    > "Not in the log, you're not." -> write
      add aff 1
    > "You're the best eyes on this ship." -> eyes
  node write narrator "I open the log at today's page and write, in my best hand: “Quill, navigator.”"
    -> stupid
  node stupid quill "That's the stupidest thing I've ever heard."
    -> underline
  node underline quill "…Underline it."
    -> sight
  node eyes quill "I know. It's nice to hear it from someone with handwriting. …So use it."
    -> write
  node sight narrator "She brings the sun down and reads it twice. Then she lays the figures on my father's line. They agree."
    -> sworn
  node sworn quill "The Old Nail lines up with the gap. Your needle lines up with the Old Nail. I'll swear to it. Tell her she has a navigator."
    > "I'll tell her." -> END
      take sextant
      set quill_navigator
    > "Tell her yourself. You've earned the look on her face." -> earned
      take sextant
      set quill_navigator
      add aff 1
  node earned quill "I'll tell her. You tell the bosun. He likes you better. You haven't stepped on his feet."
  # On the quarterdeck, once she's navigator.
  node nav quill "Navigator. It's in the log, in a clerk's hand. So it must be true."
    > "Will you show me the stars?" if not night_watch -> tonight
    > "You've been crying." if vane_convinced -> salt
    > "What happens at the reef?" if not vane_convinced -> reef
    > "Carry on, navigator." -> carry
  node tonight quill "Tonight. I keep the watch on deck now. Come down in the dark and I'll show you a bearing."
    > "I'll dress for the cold. …For the cold, I mean." -> carry
  node reef quill "If she says yes, I steer and you shout at a compass. If she says no, we take the long way and never find out."
    > "Then she'll have to say yes." -> carry
  node salt quill "It's the sextant. It's got salt in it. …Get to the bow, cargo. I'll be on the wheel."
  node carry quill "Go on. I've a sky to check, and it's bigger than you."
